set<vector<pair<int,int>>> distinctShapes;

Think of it as:

set
 ↓
automatically compares shapes
 ↓
same shape → one copy
different shape → separate entry

Whereas unordered_set would need:

unordered_set
      ↓
needs hash(vector<pair<int,int>>)
      ↓
you must write that hash

Rule of thumb:
For competitive programming, if your object is something like vector<pair<int,int>>, set is often the easiest choice unless you specifically want unordered_set and are comfortable writing a custom hash.